---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { site } from "../data/site";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Why A Rap Blog exists, how its recommendations work, and the standards behind every listening path."
>
  <header class="page-hero">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">About the publication</p>
      <h1>You are not late. You just need a route.</h1>
      <p>
        {site.name} is for people who still love rap but no longer know where to begin. It replaces
        the infinite feed with a small number of argued, sequenced recommendations.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>
  <section class="content-section">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="info-grid">
        <article class="info-card">
          <p class="kicker">01 / Point of view</p>
          <h2>A guide, not a database</h2>
          <p>
            These articles make choices. They explain why one record follows another rather than
            pretending every option is equally useful.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="info-card">
          <p class="kicker">02 / Experience</p>
          <h2>Honest about the source</h2>
          <p>
            Personal listening is presented as opinion. Historical and factual claims are sourced.
            Products not personally owned are never described as tested.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="info-card">
          <p class="kicker">03 / Independence</p>
          <h2>Recommendations come first</h2>
          <p>
            Commercial relationships are disclosed before monetized links. A commission never buys
            a place on a listening path.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
      <div class="legal-copy author-note">
        <h2>Who is vestige?</h2>
        <p>
          vestige is the pen name behind A Rap Blog: a longtime listener writing for people
          who recognize the feeling of loving the music while falling behind its pace. The name
          keeps the focus on the route rather than the résumé.
        </p>
        <p>
          Questions, corrections, or a path you want mapped? Email
          <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .author-note {
    margin-top: 5rem;
  }
</style>
